# Build context for the Next.js image. The Dockerfile runs `COPY . .` after
# `npm ci`, so without this file the context drags node_modules, .next and the
# whole docs tree into the build.
#
# Nothing below is needed to build or run the app. Verified: the build reads
# src/, public/ (llms.txt, which is .txt), the config files and
# scripts/gen-lastmod.mjs. No code path reads any .md, docs/ or plans/.

# Dependencies and build output are created inside the image.
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. These must never reach an image layer. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# inlined at build time, so pass those as build args rather than shipping .env.
.env
.env.*
.cron-secret.txt

# Version control.
.git

# Documentation and one-off artefacts.
# Note: public/README.md is Next.js scaffold boilerplate, not an asset. It is
# unreferenced but is served on the live site today (/README.md returns 200).
# Excluding it here only affects the Docker image. It should be deleted from
# public/ separately so the live site stops serving it too.
**/*.md
docs
plans
_capture

# Deleted from the repo in the same pass as this file. Kept here so they cannot
# return to the build context if either directory is ever restored.
mirrors
graphify-out